    "narrative": "Ghost Ride the WHIP enters today\u2019s slate with **Corbin Carroll** standing as our undisputed anchor. With an elite score of 87.14, he benefits from a premier matchup against Mikolas, and the combination of an aggressive base projection and the high probability of a stolen base\u2014aided by the opposing pitcher's slow delivery\u2014makes him our top offensive engine. **Gabriel Moreno** and **Austin Riley** also grade out as strong starts (70.58 and 71.27, respectively). While **Austin Riley** is hitting lower in the order, his park factors are significantly elevated, and the opponent's tendency to allow stolen bases provides a unique ceiling for an infielder. **Isaac Paredes** rounds out our top-tier group, maximizing his dynamic platoon advantage against Fedde to push his score comfortably into the 70s.\n\nWe are navigating a few high-risk profiles today, most notably with **Josh Naylor**, whose projection is heavily suppressed by a difficult draw against deGrom. Despite the unfavorable SP_xERA, **Josh Naylor** remains in the UTIL slot because his floor is higher than our remaining bench options. The most interesting bench decision today involved **Seiya Suzuki**, who narrowly missed the cut at 47.00. While his 8th-order slot is favorable, the combination of a tough SP_xERA from Ashcraft and our focus on elite speed as the scarcest category pushed us to prioritize the lineup efficiency of **Jose Caballero** and **Henry Bolte**, despite the latter\u2019s lower base score. \n\nFinally, managers should monitor the volatility at the bottom of the order. **Jose Caballero** and **Henry Bolte** are currently hovering near our \"marginal\" threshold. While **Jose Caballero** is hindered by a tough matchup against S\u00e1nchez, his speed remains vital to our 5x5 strategy; however, if he were to fall out of the lineup or if defensive adjustments against his steal attempts intensify, we will look to rotate **Zach McKinstry** or **Edwin Arroyo** into future sets. We are closely watching the weather and confirming that **Vinnie Pasquantino** remains sidelined, as his absence continues to force us into sub-optimal bench depth configurations.",
